\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Boost geometry in the $t,x$ plane, with $x={\bm  {\mathrm  {u}}}\cdot {\bm  {\mathrm  {r}}}\in \mathbb  {R}$. The cyan primed axes have rapidity $\theta =0.8$. The vector ${U}={L}^{-2}$ is the primed frame's unit time direction, expressed in the original coordinates; its components lie on the black unit-determinant hyperbola. The boost takes this vector to rest while preserving the light directions. The cyan unit-norm circle is not preserved. Right: $\det {U}=1$ for every rapidity, whereas $\lVert {U}\rVert ^2=\cosh (2\theta )$ changes.}}{28}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:boost-geometry}{{1}{28}{Boost geometry in the $t,x$ plane, with $x=\bu \dotprod \br \in \R $. The cyan primed axes have rapidity $\theta =0.8$. The vector $\pU =\pL ^{-2}$ is the primed frame's unit time direction, expressed in the original coordinates; its components lie on the black unit-determinant hyperbola. The boost takes this vector to rest while preserving the light directions. The cyan unit-norm circle is not preserved. Right: $\det \pU =1$ for every rapidity, whereas $\lVert \pU \rVert ^2=\cosh (2\theta )$ changes}{figure.1}{}}
\citation{tong-relativity}
